('Hotel','35',35,'Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving Hotel to Old City    - Old City tour starts from Shamakhi Gates followed by below places (Photo stop):  - Shamakhi Gates – The historic entrance to the Old City, showcasing iconic stone architecture.  - Sculptures of Azim Azimzadeh – Artistic monuments honoring Azerbaijan’s famed satirical painter and graphic artist.  - Caravanserai of Bukhara – A restored medieval inn once used by Silk Road traders for rest and trade.  - Caravanserai of Multani – A traditional guesthouse built for merchants from Multan, reflecting oriental caravan culture.  - Maiden’s Tower – Baku’s mysterious UNESCO-listed tower offering panoramic views of the Old City.  - Bazar Square – A lively historic square once serving as the commercial heart of Icherisheher.  - Miniature Books’ Museum – A unique museum displaying one of the world’s largest collections of tiny books.  - Shirvanshahs’ Palace – A majestic 15th-century royal complex showcasing medieval Azerbaijani architecture.   13:00 – Lunch Break   14:00 – Visit the Heydar Aliyev Centre  - Visit to Heydar Aliyev Center & “I LOVE BAKU” sign Photostop  - If it’s first time of your arrival to Baku, just be aware of that   from the bird view you can clearly see the Heydar Aliyev’s   Signature on the Heydar Aliyev’s Center design. It’s a wave-like  building rises from a bed of concrete. Its immobile white walls   look as though they have been frozen mid-ripple. The abstract   architecture is unlike anything else in the capital city. The   Heydar Aliyev Center, which was designed by renowned architect Zaha Hadid.   18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)   19:00 –Drop to Hotel   Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',35.0),
